-- The offset must be a non-negative integer: not NULL, Nullable, fractional or a string
-- lag and lead do not accept an explicit frame; lagInFrame and leadInFrame do
0	0	1
1	0	2
2	1	0
-- The default must be compatible with the value type; a NULL default makes the result Nullable
0	\N	Nullable(UInt64)
1	0	Nullable(UInt64)
2	1	Nullable(UInt64)
-- Several offsets in one query, with and without defaults
0	0	0	100	1	2	3
1	0	0	100	2	3	4
2	1	0	100	3	4	100
3	2	1	0	4	0	100
4	3	2	1	0	0	100
-- Offsets larger than the partition give the default
0	0	-1
1	0	-1
2	0	-1
-- Offsets larger than one block
0	0	5000
-- Offsets reaching the partition edge when partitions are not aligned to blocks
0	0	5000
-- Sparse rows after a filter see their true neighbours
0	0	11
-- lag and lead agree with lagInFrame and leadInFrame over an unbounded frame
0	0	3000
